WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.467
-You look fantastic.
-Let me take this off.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.601
-Would you like me to hold
your jacket?

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.634
-Sure, thank you, Jimmy.
That's very nice of you.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.501
-Absolutely.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:07.968
Welcome back to our show,
Aubrey.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.434
I've missed you.
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.100
-I know, it has been too long.
-You've been busy, busy, busy.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.834
-I know.
-You just got back from Italy.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.033
-That's right.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.634
-You're filming the new season
of "White Lotus."

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.400
-That's right, "White Lotus."

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:20.634
-Oh, yeah!

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:23.200
Whoo! I cannot wait for this.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.434
It's very secretive, obviously.
-Yes.

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.868
-But I'm a big fan
of the first one.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:30.801
And we all love Mike White
and Jennifer Coolidge.

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.434
And so here's the description
of your character.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.100
-Yeah.
-Hopefully, no spoilers.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.400
You ready?
-Okay.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.834
-A woman on vacation with
her husband and his friends.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:40.834
There you go.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:41.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.567
Thank you for that.
No spoilers.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:44.868
-Yes.
-Wow.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:47.000
-I am playing against type.
-Wow. [ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.567
That's amazing.
-Big time.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.000
-Yeah, you're always typecast.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.000
You're always the woman
who's not on vacation.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.334
-Exactly.
I would never do that.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:56.868
-You would never go on vacation
with your husband

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.100
and his friends?
-Nuh-uh. No.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.534
-Uh-uh.
-No, no, no.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.400
-How did you end up
working on this?

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.234
-Mike and I -- actually, we've
been friends for a long time.

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.000
So, we were trying to come up

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.601
with something else to do
together,

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.033
and then the pandemic happened.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:13.100
And we ended up -- and then,
he just ended up, you know,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.200
bringing me to the party.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.367
-I can see you guys totally
working --

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.567
-It was crazy.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.133
I mean, you've been out there
for five months?

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:20.267
-Five months.
Yeah, that's a really long time.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.334
-Yeah. Do you speak Italian?

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:25.567
-Si, parlo Italiano --
Parlo un po Italiano.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.934
-Grazie mille.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.133
- Si. Yeah, but I was out there
for five months.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.133
The show's epic.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:35.801
There's all kinds of --
everyone kept getting COVID,

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.667
so we kept kind of, like --
you know?

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:41.033
And then before that, I was
shooting a movie in Italy.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.000
Another -- a different thing
called "Spin Me Around,"

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.934
which is coming out this month,
that my husband directed.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:49.400
So, I've really been in Italy
for like almost a year

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.200
if you, like,
put it all together.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:52.567
-Let's talk about
"Emily the Criminal."

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:53.901
-Okay.
-You also produced it.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:54.934
-I did.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.934 --> 00:01:56.033
-That's why I wear
the big jacket.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.601
-Yeah, exactly.
-'Cause every talk show,

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:59.033
I'm going to get a bigger
and bigger jacket

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.467
until it's on
the God damn floor.

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.367
-I'm ready to -- I'm ready to --
Yeah.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.934
-I'm going to come out with
a big cigar in my mouth.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.000
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.467
-Remember movies?

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.234
-Yeah, you want to produce
some movies?

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.834
-Yeah, you want me to produce
your movie?

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.234
Give me $500,000 --
- Dollars.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:13.534
-Dollars.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.200
That's actually not enough.
-No.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.801
What is "Emily the Criminal"
about?

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:20.300
-"Emily the Criminal" is about
a woman from New Jersey,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.801
who is in L.A.,
and she is basically saddled

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:27.200
with thousands of dollars
of student loans and debt,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.834
which I think we can all relate
to, or at least a lot of us.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:31.400
-Sadly, yes.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.434
-Yeah, right?

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.968
And so, she's kind of drowning
in debt.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.567
She has a criminal record.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.033
You know, she did some stuff.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.033
You know?

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.334
Sometimes you do some stuff.

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:45.300
And -- but she can't get a job.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.801
-And she's -- she basically is
tipped off to do this kind of

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:53.567
illegal crime thing.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.267
Like a scam kind of thing.

00:02:55.267 --> 00:02:57.968
And it's a petty crime,
but it's still illegal.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.901
And she finds out she's kind of
good at it.

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:04.701
And so, she kind of, you know,
goes down that path and becomes,

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.534
you know, the criminal.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.667
-You got to do
some action scenes which..

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.334
-I did.
-I like seeing Aubrey Plaza

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.934
doing action.
-Yeah, thank you very much.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:13.634
-And I was -- I was wondering.

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.868
I said, "Would you every do more
action things?

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.601
You go, "That's funny you asked,
James.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:20.434
Because I'm on the cover of
'Movie Maker Magazine.'"

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.467
-I am.
-Which -- look at this.

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.801
-There I am.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:27.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.601
That's right. "Movie Maker."

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.400
-You're on the cover of
"Movie Maker" magazine.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.467
-Yeah, I -- they asked me to be
on the cover of "Vogue,"

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.167
but I said, no, I'm doing
"Movie Maker."

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.133
-That's right.
You tell them what's up.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.501
-So --
-This is the one. "Movie Maker."

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.567
-So, take that.

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:39.934
-That's exactly what you want
to be on.

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:43.367
But then, your friend, is it --
-Yeah, so, my friend,

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.767
Edgar Wright, actually saw that
and texted me

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:49.033
and said, "Oh, my God,
You're the new Lara Croft?

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:50.400
You're the new 'Tomb Raider?'"

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.801
That's the character in --
and I was like, "No, Edgar.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.934
That's my movie,
'Emily the Criminal.'"

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:58.501
And he genuinely thought I was
cast as the new "Tomb Raider."

00:03:58.501 --> 00:03:59.634
-He thought
that was a gun holster.

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.434
That's not a gun,
that's just a purse.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.100
-That's a purse, yeah.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.133
And then -- exactly.
Exactly.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.601
-But I can see it.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:07.601
I can see this happening.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:08.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:10.667
-Yeah. I know.

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.734
-I can actually see
this happening.

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:14.067
-Right? I know.
-Yes.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.868
-It's funny because I didn't
actually -- and then,

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:17.701
I looked it up and I was like,
they are actually --

00:04:17.701 --> 00:04:19.834
they are casting
this role right now.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.167
And I was like,
"Well, there you go.

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:22.667
The new 'Tomb Raider.'
Whatever."

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.100
-There you go.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.834
-Right?
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.934
Here's Aubrey Plaza
in "Emily the Criminal."

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.367
Take a look at this.

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:32.234
-We just need to go back to
the office for just a second.

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.767
-Why? What's wrong?

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:35.167
-Nothing. We forgot one thing.

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:37.868
It's just -- it's my fault.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:40.167
-You can't tell me what it is?

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:41.534
-It's not big deal, you know?

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:45.033
So, just -- can you turn off
the engine, please?

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:49.067
Turn off the engine.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.434
-Hey, hey. No!

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.234
[ Horn honks, woman screams ]

00:04:58.234 --> 00:05:00.434
[ Man grunts ]

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:01.534
-[ Hyperventilating ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.467
[ Engine revs ]

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.567
-Wow.
-Aubrey Plaza.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.300
"Emily the Criminal"
is in theaters this Friday.

